markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Common CSS Properties

####  CSS properties tell the computer how each HTML element should look and behave, including color, spacing, and layout that bring the page’s structure to life.

<table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin-bottom:24px; font-size:14pt;">
  <tr style="background:#f2f2f2;">
    <th colspan="3" style="padding:10px; text-align:left;">🎨 Text & Color</th>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">color</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">Text color</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;"><code>color: blue;</code></td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background:#fafafa;">
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">background-color</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">Fill behind content</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;"><code>background-color: lightblue;</code></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">font-size</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">Text size</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;"><code>font-size: 18px;</code></td>
  </tr>
  <tr style="background:#fafafa;">
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">font-family</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">Font style</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;"><code>font-family: Arial;</code></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">text-align</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">Horizontal text alignment</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;"><code>text-align: center;</code></td>
  </tr>
</table>
<br>

<table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin-bottom:24px; font-size:14pt;">
  <tr style="background:#f2f2f2;">
    <th colspan="3" style="padding:10px; text-align:left;">📏 Spacing & Size</th>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">margin</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">Outside spacing</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;"><code>margin: 20px;</code></td>
  </tr>

  <tr style="background:#fafafa;">
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">padding</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">Inside spacing</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;"><code>padding: 16px;</code></td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">border</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">Outline</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;"><code>border: 2px solid black;</code></td>
  </tr>

  <tr style="background:#fafafa;">
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">width</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">Element width</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;"><code>width: 300px;</code></td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">height</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">Element height</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;"><code>height: 200px;</code></td>
  </tr>
</table>
<br>
<table style="width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin-bottom:24px; font-size:14pt;">
  <tr style="background:#f2f2f2;">
    <th colspan="3" style="padding:10px; text-align:left;">🧭 Layout & Alignment</th>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">display</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">Sets layout mode</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;"><code>display: flex;</code></td>
  </tr>

  <tr style="background:#fafafa;">
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">justify-content</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">Horizontal alignment</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;"><code>justify-content: center;</code></td>
  </tr>

  <tr>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">align-items</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">Vertical alignment</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;"><code>align-items: center;</code></td>
  </tr>

  <tr style="background:#fafafa;">
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">gap</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;">Space between items</td>
    <td style="padding:8px;font-size:14pt;"><code>gap: 12px;</code></td>
  </tr>
</table>



>#### Do you recognize any of the properties from the previous level?

## Remember you are just getting started.

#### These are just a few properties to give you context. 

#### It’s not important yet to know how every line of code works, but to see the big picture and communicate clearly with the AI about what you want your page to do.

#### As you move into the next level, focus on **prompting the AI to produce the outcome you desire.** 

<div style="background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 40px; color: #000000; width: 95%; padding: 1px 20px 1px 20px;">

<p style="line-height: 1.5; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; margin-top: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-size: 18px; "><b> 💡Remember: </b>The goal of this unit is to help students clearly communicate their ideas to AI in order to create the website they envision, not learn every detail of HTML or CSS.
</p>
</div>



MARKDOWN
